  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>F</mtext> <mo>-</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mtext>O</mtext> </mrow> </math> are weak field ligands so pairing of electrons in metal cations 3d subshell will not take place.</p><p>now we have to cosider hybridization that is given in following diagram.<br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/f7126c31-2243-4e52-9082-cea3fa574970-image.png\"/><br/><u><strong>​</strong></u><br ><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext>μ</mtext><mtext>P</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mtext>BM</mtext></math></p><p><br ><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext>μ</mtext><mtext>Q</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mtext>BM</mtext></math></p><p><br ><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext>μ</mtext><mtext>R</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>6</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></msqrt><mtext>BM</mtext></math><br ><math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>μ</mtext> <mtext>Q</mtext> </msub> <mo><</mo> <msub> <mtext>μ</mtext> <mtext>R</mtext> </msub> <mo><</mo> <msub> <mtext>μ</mtext> <mtext>P</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </math><br ><math> <mrow> <mtext>Q < R < P</mtext> </mrow> </math></p>",
